# Agent routing (this repo)

Delegate to project subagents in `.cursor/agents/` when work is clearly in one domain. All write agents have **git + terminal** (`readonly: false`).

| Path / topic | Subagent | Auto rules (globs) |
|--------------|----------|-------------------|
| `src/main/java/**/service/collector/**`, `model/**`, collectors | `collector-backend` | `metrics-collector-architecture`, `docker`, `payload` |
| `src/main/resources/static/**`, `src/main/java/**/web/**` | `dashboard-ui` | `metrics-collector-ui` |
| `src/main/java/**/hub/**`, `hub.html`, push/ingest | `hub-platform` | — |
| `src/test/**`, `Makefile`, `tool/**`, `.github/**` | `test-ci` | — |
| Pre-merge / "doğrula" / verify | `verifier` | readonly |

## How to assign work

- **Automatic**: Open or @-mention files in a folder — scoped `.mdc` rules attach via `globs`.
- **Explicit**: In chat: *"Use collector-backend for MacNetworkUsageParser"* or *"@collector-backend fix parser"*.
- **Parallel**: Independent domains (e.g. UI + hub test) → launch two subagents in parallel.

## Do not

- Split one small change across multiple agents.
- Bypass council gate (`council-gate.mdc`) — stop and ask user if V1–V20 would be violated.

See `.cursor/agents/README.md` for full setup.
